2021 was a banner year for science  fiction movies filled to the brim with  kaiju showdowns time loop extravaganzas  and classic franchise fare here's the  question though just how many of these  excellent sci-fi movies have you seen  fish is a movie that blends romance and  drama with the world of science fiction  released in theaters and on streaming  services in february 2021 director chad  hartigan's movie is set in seattle in  the near future in the midst of an  epidemic of an alzheimer's-like illness  known as nia olivia cooke and jack  o'connell star as emma and jude a couple  struggling with the effect of nia on  their relationship and society  littlefish was filmed before covet 19  and was due to be shown at the cancelled  2020 tribeca film festival this means  that its underlying premise is  coincidental but incredibly timely too  entertainment weekly's mary celosi  writes that despite the subject matter  little fish resonates mostly as a love  story she also praises the performances  from cook and o'connell writing they  both bring the cool project a necessary  warmth that sells their relationship  which is the real star here a number of  critics have noted the film's  resemblance to 2004's eternal sunshine  of the spotless mind though this movie  still has its own unique charms celosi  says the sci-fi trapping gives the  film's central question a poetic shape  while jordan rob of the film stage notes  that the details of emotional bonds are  given utmost priority in the story over  extraneous exposition related to light  sci-fi touches  in other words if you're looking for a  love story fit for these trying times  little fish might be the one for you  take a little romance a little sci-fi  and the basic premise of groundhog day  and you've got the map of tiny perfect  things the plot finds kyle allen as mark  a smart teenager stuck in a time loop  who meets catherine newton's margaret  another teenager stuck in the same loop  the two subsequently decide to focus on  finding the tiny perfect things of their  endlessly repeating day released on  amazon prime video in february 2021 the  map of tiny perfect things gathered good  notices for its strong cast and its  emotional resonance mike ward at should  i see it writes this is a detail-driven  meticulously crafted film that stands  apart from its peers with two strong  lead performances a bit of a mischievous  grin and heart firmly entrenched on its  sleeve meanwhile shawnee harris of  culturists says the map of tiny perfect  things is a new spin on young love that  will stimulate your mind and touch your  heart  if you're looking for some superheroes  with your sci-fi then zack snyder's  justice league is here to save the day  this epic hbo max adventure which clocks  in at a mere 4 hours and 2 minutes may  have been met with a mixed reaction from  the critics but dc's fans couldn't  possibly be happier plot-wise the film  is broadly similar to the 2017 movie  justice league superman's sacrifice and  dawn of justice has spurred bats to  unite a team of his super friends to  face off against a major cosmic threat i  don't care how many demons he's fought  and how many hells  he's never fought us  [Music]  not us united  the movie has six chapters and an  epilogue for easier viewing and  characters such as cyborg and the flash  have their stories significantly fleshed  out giving the film a grander scale with  deeper meaning the ages jake wilson  writes this is genuinely a different  film from the earlier justice league and  a much more coherent one a running theme  in the critical response to the  so-called snyder cut is that zack  snyder's strongest and weakest  tendencies are both on display despite  agreeing that the movie earns its  self-importance vultures bilga of b  renotes when you get the best of snyder  you also get the worst  meanwhile gary mcconaughey of glasgow  live says it's big it's brash and it's  bombastic  so if you love dc comics and you love  zack snyder you're sure as heck gonna  love this  launching on hulu back in march 2021  boss level features a hyper violent time  loop a ton of action and frank grillo  playing a badass former special forces  agent what more could you possibly want  in this case roy pulver's loop involves  reliving the day on which he meets a  grisly death forcing him to figure out  who killed him and why so that he can  end the loop and rescue his family in  order to do so he has to find mel  gibson's colonel ventor and avoid a  whole army of killers along the way  grillo in particular drew a lot of  praise for his leading role in boss  level richard roper of the chicago sun  times complements grillo's ability to  carry the film saying that he pulls it  off with a combination of brute force  and light charm indiewire's christian  blavelt also gives grillo high marks  saying the actor gives the film a pulse  he continues he gets you to invest in  roy enough that even without a  controller in your hands you never feel  like you're simply watching someone else  play a video game  known as sunriho in its original korea  space sweepers takes place in a  dystopian 2092 the movie follows a crew  of space junk collectors who find a  robot girl named dorothy who is not only  wanted by the evil corporation uts but  can also be used as a weapon realizing  they can make a heap of money from their  discovery the sweepers hold her for  ransom which turns out to be a pretty  bad idea space weepers stars kim tari as  captain zhang and richard armitage as  uts's elon musk-like gazillionaire  sullivan south korean writer director  joe seung-hee is the man behind the  camera previously known for his 2012 hit  a werewolf boy and 2016's phantom  detective netflix released space  sweepers in february 2021 to mostly  positive reviews daniel hart at  readysteadycut writes spaceweepers is an  energetic space adventure that manages  to slightly emotionally engage the  audience while stimulating them with fun  action sequences while the strangers  charles madetti says space weepers  features lots of explosions  lots of robots and that raw examination  of capitalist class structures we have  come to expect from the best of south  korea's directors  supposedly the last installment of  legendary's monsterverse godzilla vs  kong is directed by adam wingard and  features a host of franchise newcomers  alongside returning faces such as millie  bobby brown and kyle chandler  in godzilla vs kong the gargantuan  titans have been dormant in the three  years since godzilla defeated king  ghidorah meanwhile the hollow earth  theory discussed in godzilla king of the  monsters has gained traction and the  scientific agency known as monarch has  been keeping tabs on kong on skull  island however a mysterious force  agitates godzilla into attacking the  tech organization known as apex  cybernetics and it's not long before  kong has been co-opted into searching  for the hollow earth's power source  these threads eventually converge when  godzilla's kong sense kicks in  reigniting their ancient rivalry upon  the movie's release in march 2021  critics praised the movie for its kaiju  action with critic peter travers saying  the clash of these titans is spectacular  in every sense of the word possibly the  most glowing praise however comes from  matt zoller seitz who writes that  godzilla vs kong just might be the best  studio film so far this year if it isn't  it's for damn sure the most fun as a  great man once said let them fight  an existentially fraught sci-fi drama  released on netflix stowaway sends three  astronauts to mars on a two-year mission  and then throws a major wrench into  their plans when you guessed it a  stowaway is discovered on board director  joe penna assembled a great cast for  this movie which stars tony collette as  marina barnett the ship's leader on her  final journey into space  anna kendrick plays zoe levinson the  medical researcher while daniel day kim  plays the ship's biologist david kim  unbeknownst to them shamir anderson's  michael adams is also abort albeit  unwittingly and somehow injured  unfortunately whatever caused adam's  predicament has damaged the ship's life  support controls leaving enough oxygen  for only three people in his review of  stowaway varieties owen gliebermann says  hannah takes a mission to mars and  unfurls it on a direct and intimate  emotional level we always feel the  characters could be us  meanwhile christy lemire of  rogerebert.com writes  the movie is a clever take on a familiar  genre with a terrific cast  if you're in the mood for a classic  sci-fi flick with a dark twist stowaway  could be the movie for you  the latest movie from director alexander  aja oxygen has been hailed as a taut  engaging sci-fi thriller in this netflix  french language film a woman named liz  wakes up in a cryogenic pod with amnesia  not knowing who or where she is her only  companion is milo an artificial  intelligence program who advises her  that the oxygen levels of the pod are  decreasing at an alarming rate  if liz can't figure out who she is and  why she's there she'll suffocate best  known for the gory horror of 2003's  slasher high tension and 2019's  alligator thriller crawl aja has been  praised for his restraint with this  particular sci-fi gem filmed during  coveted lockdown from a 2016 script by  christy leblanc oxygen issues the usual  viscera for a more existential sense of  dread as david rooney of the hollywood  reporter writes while cult followers of  aja's extreme horror might be let down  by his turn toward more measured sci-fi  there's plenty of creepy unease packed  into his execution of a simple scenario  that grows increasingly complicated  meanwhile brian talarico of  rogerebert.com notes that this truly  feels like the most pandemic thriller  yet in its own unpredictable way it's a  film about isolation loss and an  uncertain future  the long-awaited sequel to 2018's a  quiet place the quiet place part 2 had  its theatrical only release in may 2021  quickly earning praise from critics and  audiences alike director and  screenwriter john krasinski's  continuation of the abbott family story  also provides a glimpse of the first day  that the sonic aliens arrived allowing  the beloved actor to briefly reprise his  role as lee abbott emily blunt also  returns as evelyn abbott who journeys  with her newborn infant and two older  children in search of a new place to  live after their farm becomes  uninhabitable they eventually come  across killian murphy's emmet a  once-friendly acquaintance with links to  their past  emmett however is now withdrawn and  sullen and abbott no longer knows if she  can trust him a quiet place part 2  received praise for its tight script and  superior use of tension matthew rosa of  salon writes  the film is packed with visceral moments  that stick to your ribs  carrie darling of the houston chronicle  also points out that the film is a  crafty exercise in tension editing and  sound design that never wears out its  welcome  bloody disgusting's megan navarro has  lavished praise on deaf actress  millicent simmons in particular saying  that this is above all simmons show she  nails it so if you were worried about  whether or not this sequel would live up  to the first film rest assured it's sure  to be a terrifying treat for horror fans  the netflix sci-fi flick the mitchells  versus the machines is a kid-friendly  adventure that hit the streaming site in  april 2021 this comedy animation follows  the mitchells a dysfunctional family who  embark on a hectic road trip  unfortunately their vacation turns into  an apocalyptic battle for survival after  the beginning of a robotic revolution  the emphasis on technology as villain  grounds the film squarely in sci-fi  territory as the mitchells who've set  aside their gadgets for an old-fashioned  vacation are thrust into a digital war  the mitchells versus the machines has  been quite the hit with critics which  might come as little surprise  considering it's produced by phil lord  and christopher miller who are otherwise  known for spider-man into the  spider-verse the lego movie and 21 jump  street  bob strauss of the san francisco  chronicle calls the movie a machine  apocalypse for the whole family while  other critics have noted the film's  surprising pro-tech stance how's that  well the guardians benjamin lee writes  rather than the easier and clumsier film  director mike ryonda could have made  scolding kids for swiping and tapping  and missing out on real life he shows  that young digital creators are  achieving incredible things and that  when used right this form of  connectedness can be a powerful force  free guy stars ryan reynolds as the  titular guy a man who greets his  goldfish gets coffee and goes to his job  at the bank once he's there he talks  with his best friend security guard  buddy and this is exactly what he does  every single day as it turns out guy has  no idea he's stuck in a predetermined  loop as a non-playing character in a  popular video game that is until he  meets millie and becomes enamored millie  wants to prove video game impresario  antoine stole the game she developed so  she's looking for proof before antoine  can destroy the game and guy along with  it directed by sean levy free guy  received a number of positive reviews  from critics charlotte o'sullivan of the  evening standard praises the humor in  the movie writing the humor in free guy  is knowing rather than nasty and even at  its most surreal avoids coming across as  indulgent  while robert daniels of the playlist  simply writes free guy is a winner  filmed on an iphone during the covet 19  lockdown the themes of the british film  infant item subject unknown are both  timely and timeless  written by married couple matthew and  tory butler heart and directed by  matthew infant items stars tori as jane  an amnesiac woman trapped in a parallel  world and in a time loop to boot the  film features cameos from sir ian  mckellen as dr charles marland white and  conlet hill as professor aaron  ostergaard both of whom may have  information that could help jane regain  her memory and return to her own world  in particular infinitum subject unknown  has been praised for tory butler hart's  performance for example rachel harper at  sci-fi now writes that the actress who's  frequently alone on screen in the movie  shoulders that responsibility incredibly  well while carrie o'shea of warped  perspective says butler heart pitches it  perfectly given the situations unfolding  around her and she does most of it  without saying anything  critics have also been impressed by how  the movie tackles its heavy and horrific  themes with sarah cartland of caution  spoilers writing that  infant item is a chilling story about  the expansion of human life for a sci-fi  flick that'll satisfy your cravings for  intensity go no further than infinitum  subject unknown  james gunn scores again with his take on  dc super villains in the suicide squad  less a sequel to 2016's suicide squad  and more a reboot of the title this film  brings back harley quinn amanda waller  and a handful of other familiar faces  from the original at the same time  however it brings in a whole heap of new  characters fronted by idris elba's  bloodsport and john cena's peacemaker  once again waller offers a ragtag group  of super villains the chance to shave  time off their prison sentences by  undertaking a secret mission if they go  off script however she'll blow off their  heads cue the mayhem we're all gonna die  i hope so  the seattle times soren anderson writes  of the film  gun masterfully mixes humor and  bloodshed and manages to give a  surprising number of characters room to  develop their personas and when it comes  to staging set pieces he's at his best  while ollie richards of empire writes  when gunn took on guardians of the  galaxy he turned nonsense into gold for  marvel by giving the suicide squad the  same sense of mischief and an equally  surreal streak he's done the same for dc  frank herbert's dune has long been  considered an unfilmable science fiction  novel but that hasn't stopped people  from trying first there was the 1984  david lynch film and then the 2000  miniseries and now its latest cinematic  incarnation has arrived and it's pretty  darn good too  director denny villeneuve wisely  presents only a portion of frank  herbert's epic original novel in a way  that's both satisfying as a movie in  itself and as an introduction to the  events to come dune is set in 10 191 a  year in which house atreides is tasked  by the emperor to replace the ruthless  harkenans as overseers of the planet  arrakis harvesting its coveted spice and  keeping an eye on the indigenous fremen  the harkonnens are less than pleased  about this of course and a devastating  conflict quickly erupts timothy chalamet  stars as protagonist paul artradis the  son of duke leto artradis and his  consort lady jessica artradis he leads a  cast that includes such stars as zendaya  dave bautista and jason momoa audiences  and critics alike have fallen in love  with denny villeneuve's dune for example  salon's melanie mcfarland writes  it is a gorgeous sensory immersion that  holds us in its spell for hours with an  ending that sparks yearning to see what  comes next  meanwhile the av club's ignati  vishnovetsky notes that although the  story may feel inconclusive the  resulting film is a rarity among the  over long effects heavy blockbusters of  the last decade one actually wishes it  didn't have to end so soon  in director miguel sapochnick's finch  which hit apple tv plus in november 2021  a solar flare has scorched the earth  turning the planet into a  post-apocalyptic nightmare tom hanks's  finch weinberg a robotics engineer has  managed to survive along with his helper  bot dewey and dog goodyear unfortunately  finch is dying to ensure his pooch's  survival after his death finch creates a  new robot to care for him this robot  chooses jeff for its name  but after finch's work is interrupted  jeff is left with the same developmental  stage as a child it's then up to fence  to parent jeff so that he can grow and  care for goodyear finch is tailor-made  for people who love dogs children robots  and tom hanks and it's also a really  gorgeous movie thomas lafley of variety  praises the movie's visuals adding finch  offers the right kind of big budget  cinematic escape to viewers young and  old one that's as endearingly uplifting  and disarming as a devoted good boy's  unconditional company as you might  expect hanks is phenomenal with the  austin chronicles richard whittaker  writing if there is a cinematic  embodiment of hope it may well be tom  hanks  as you may have heard many of the  reviews for marvel studios superhero  epic eternals weren't exactly great  sometimes though you have to disregard a  lousy score on rotten tomatoes and go  with your heart or in this case the  audience score which stands at an  impressive 80 percent academy  award-winning director chloe zhao  grounds this cosmic tale of race of  immortal beings in basic human emotions  such as love and sacrifice the ten  eternals arrive on earth to defeat the  deviants aliens who are hell-bent on  destruction once that's done the  eternals remain to observe and  occasionally assist humanity throughout  history but they're instructed by their  celestial leader ereshim not to  interfere in human affairs however  thousands of years of observing the  worst of human behavior begins to wear  on some eternals and when aresham  finally reveals the eternal's true  purpose in nature all hell breaks loose  it's worth bearing in mind that not all  critics slammed this film nina lee combs  of the chicago reader says eternals is a  genuine delightful character development  nestled inside of a complex and  challenging narrative speaking in  defense of the film peter travers of abc  news writes what you'll remember is the  quiet at the heart of the storm and the  intimate connections that zhao values  above spectacle different you bet but  it's also what makes eternals unique and  unforgettable  spider-man no way home earned a  sparkling slate of reviews and reached  dizzying heights in box office revenue  in record time in this installment in  the mcu peter parker's identity has been  revealed to the world forcing immense  pressure onto parker and his friends and  family with nowhere else to go parker  asks dr strange for help and  inadvertently tears open the walls of  the multiverse hello peter  [Music]  spider-man no way home has received  especially high marks for being a film  both die hard fans and casual film goers  can enjoy carrie darling of the houston  chronicle wrote no way home is a deft  funny and surprisingly emotional  superhero adventure that manages to  provide both fan service for the marvel  faithful and breezy entertainment for  those who wouldn't know peter parker  from peter jackson empire's dan joellen  offered similar praise and added that it  won't just make you cheer it'll make you  want to hug your friends too  in the german sci-fi romance i'm your  man marin eggert stars as alma an  archaeologist who agrees to participate  in a unique three-week study  the product being evaluated is a robot  named tom who has been programmed to be  her perfect match depending on alma's  verdict tom and others like him could be  granted human rights can artificially  intelligent beings fulfill the romantic  needs of someone who's single should  such robots have freedom and can alma  even begin to answer those questions  the deep ambition that fuels i'm your  man has been rewarded with widespread  acclaim  stephanie zakirek of time magazine says  i'm your man is funny in such a gentle  way that you may not realize how  piercing it is until after the credits  have rolled  the av clubs a a dowd also praised the  cast for keeping the balance of frothy  to thoughtful right where it should be  this unique film has more on its mind  than whether the girl gets the boy and  is all the better for it  in the matrix resurrections director  lana wachowski returns to the dystopia  of the matrix keanu reeves is back as  thomas anderson this time working as a  famous game developer whose most popular  creation is a video game called the  matrix but mr anderson keeps flashing  back to another life while his therapist  tries to keep him grounded in reality  it's not long before neo is back in the  real world and eager to search for his  true love carrie anne moss's trinity  trinity believes she is tiffany however  a normal mother and wife and it's up to  neo to free her from this new life the  matrix resurrections could easily have  been a soulless cash grab but instead  it's a deeply romantic and hopeful film  that deconstructs nostalgia and explores  complex ideas such as choice and purpose  fox's emily vanderverf praised the film  for its nuanced portrayal of trauma  while noel d lilly of the chicago reader  wrote the matrix resurrections is a  breath of fresh air in a time when  reboots are a dime a dozen  director cion sono's gore-soaked  sensibilities are on full display in  prisoners of the ghostland nicholas cage  gives a superb performance as hero a  criminal who is forced by the governor  of samurai town to rescue a kidnapped  girl named bernice from the mysterious  ghostland this unique movie mashes up  science fiction western grit dystopian  drama horror and samurai cinema into one  completely unforgettable experience  while some critics found this collision  of genre a little much others praised  prisoners of the ghost land for its  sheer audacity the independence clarice  lockri said  sono may indulge in madness but it's not  madness without reason megan navarro of  bloody disgusting writes prisoners of  the ghostland is a neon drenched  spaghetti western full of idiosyncratic  humor and violent social messaging a  triumph for bizarro cinema  the film has also received kudos for his  commitment to an out there storyline  while screen daily's tim grierson  praised cage's performance as the  high-spirited heart of the production  although it's not for the faint-hearted  prisoners of the ghostland is very much  a thrill ride worth taking check out one  of our newest videos right here plus  even more looper videos about your  favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

